# Architecture Rules

The engine is modular. Respect subsystem boundaries.

## Core Modules

- Core
- Renderer
- Physics
- Scripting
- Asset Pipeline
- Editor
- HephaestusUI

## Hard Rules

- No circular dependencies
- Renderer code stays in Renderer
- Editor must not depend on runtime systems
- Core must remain lightweight

## Modification Rules

- Extend existing modules instead of creating new ones
- Do not move code between modules without instruction

## Subsystem Protection

Do NOT:
- Merge subsystems
- Rewrite rendering architecture
- Change asset pipeline structure
- Replace scripting system

If a change affects multiple systems:
- Ask the user before proceeding

---

# UI System Rules

The default UI framework for the Hephaestus Engine is **Qt**.

## Core Rules

- Unless explicitly stated otherwise, ALL UI work must use Qt.
- Assume Qt is the primary and preferred UI system.

## Restrictions

- Do NOT modify HTML-based UI systems unless explicitly requested.
- Do NOT modify ImGui-based UI systems unless explicitly requested.
- Do NOT convert UI systems between frameworks.

## UI Change Requests

When a UI change is requested:

- Default to Qt implementation.
- If the existing UI is not Qt:
  - Ask the user before modifying it.
  - Do not assume migration is desired.

## Safety Rule

If unclear which UI system is being used:
- Ask the user before making changes.
- Do not guess or rewrite UI implementations.

## Summary

- Qt is the default
- HTML and ImGui are opt-in only
- Never touch non-Qt UI unless explicitly instructed